%% Text double-tap edit request sequence
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor User as User pointer
  participant Surface as CanvasSurface
  participant Tools as CanvasToolPort
  participant IE as InteractionEngine
  participant ReadPort as InteractionReadPort
  participant Store as DocumentStoreKernel
  participant Spatial as SpatialKernel
  participant Geometry as GeometryPolicy
  participant Requests as CanvasTextEditRequested stream
  participant Frame as FrameEngine
  participant Signals as Public state/effects
  participant App as Application
  participant TextOverlay as Flutter text editor overlay app-owned

  User->>Surface: first tap on canvas
  Surface->>Tools: handlePointer(CanvasPointerSample down/up)
  Tools->>IE: normalized finite tap sample
  IE->>IE: admit tap if no active pointer conflict, stale token, or drag beyond tapSlop
  IE->>IE: convert viewPosition to finite worldPosition
  IE->>Spatial: query point hit candidates at worldPosition
  Spatial-->>IE: committed content handles in hit order
  IE->>Geometry: exact point hit for visible selectable content elements
  Geometry-->>IE: top visible selectable content element or none

  alt first tap has no top hit or top hit is not text
    IE-->>Tools: finish tap without edit request
    Note over IE,Signals: No document, revision, spatial, projection, resource, selection, preview, repaint, or action effect is produced.
  else first tap top hit is text
    IE->>ReadPort: read immutable text candidate facts
    ReadPort->>Store: read text element snapshot and boundsWorld
    Store-->>ReadPort: textSnapshot, boundsWorld, and element generation
    ReadPort-->>IE: textSnapshot, boundsWorld, and element generation
    IE->>IE: store pending tap candidate, timestamp, viewPosition, and worldPosition
    Note over IE: Pending tap state is gesture detection only. It is not document, selection, or preview state.
  end

  User->>Surface: second tap on canvas
  Surface->>Tools: handlePointer(CanvasPointerSample down/up)
  Tools->>IE: normalized finite tap sample
  IE->>IE: admit tap if no active pointer conflict, stale token, or drag beyond tapSlop
  IE->>IE: convert viewPosition to finite worldPosition
  IE->>Spatial: query point hit candidates at second worldPosition
  Spatial-->>IE: committed content handles in hit order
  IE->>Geometry: exact point hit for visible selectable content elements
  Geometry-->>IE: top visible selectable content element or none

  alt no top hit, top hit is not text, no matching pending first tap, delay exceeded, slop exceeded, or candidate changed
    IE->>IE: replace or clear pending tap candidate
    IE-->>Tools: finish tap without edit request
    Note over IE,Signals: No automatic select/deselect, preview update, repaint request, CanvasActionCommitted, or edit commit occurs.
  else top hit is text and double-tap matches the same current text element
    IE->>ReadPort: read current text edit facts
    ReadPort->>Store: read current text element snapshot, boundsWorld, and generation
    Store-->>ReadPort: current textSnapshot and boundsWorld
    ReadPort-->>IE: current textSnapshot and boundsWorld
    IE->>IE: verify candidate still visible, selectable, text, and generation-current
    IE->>Requests: emit CanvasTextEditRequested(elementId, timestampMs, viewPosition, worldPosition, boundsWorld, textSnapshot)
    Requests->>Signals: publish text edit request notification only
    Signals-->>App: deliver CanvasTextEditRequested
    App->>TextOverlay: create and own Flutter text editor overlay
    Note over App,TextOverlay: IME, focus, accessibility, text selection, hide/show policy, and editor lifetime belong to the application.
    Note over IE,Frame: The engine does not create or own the Flutter text editor overlay and does not write app overlay state into CanvasPreviewState.
    IE-->>Tools: clear pending tap candidate and finish double-tap handling
  end

  opt later application text change outside this sequence
    Note over App: The application commits changed text through updateElement(CanvasTextElementUpdate) on the normal public edit path.
  end

  Note over IE,Signals: Forbidden in this sequence: EditKernel commit, DraftDocument, TouchedSet, CommitPlan, atomic install, document or revision changes, spatial updates, projection/cache eviction, resource changes, preview mutation, selection mutation, CanvasActionCommitted, and engine-owned app overlay.
